    {
      "id": "kqi4614",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "ELECTION COMMISSION OF INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 324 of the Constitution provides for an independent Election Commission of India to direct and control elections.",
        "The ECI conducts elections to Parliament, State Legislatures, and offices of the President and Vice-President.",
        "The Chief Election Commissioner and other Election Commissioners hold equal powers and draw equal salary equivalent to a SC judge.",
        "The CEC can only be removed from office in the same manner and on same grounds as a Supreme Court judge.",
        "The Constitution has not debarred retiring Election Commissioners from further appointment by the government."
      ],
      "id": "e9ufp3r"
    },
